// Named-field policy against an MCP-generated Cedar schema.
//
// Exercises the full new pipeline:
//   - Schema generated from an MCP tool manifest via
//     cedar-policy-mcp-schema-generator
//   - Named-field predicate syntax (field: value)
//   - Implicit wildcarding of unmentioned fields
//   - Cross-action reference (CallTool as a prerequisite)
//
// Semantics: permit a transfer_funds call if the same principal
// made any transfer from the same account within the last hour.
// Uses the bare predicate form (no output matching) since the
// MCP-generated schema puts output in the context, not as a
// Temporal output: clause.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"transfer_funds",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"transfer_funds"::request{ input.from_account: context.input.from_account }
};
